To sign your flash.bin manually, make use of install_uboot_imx8.sh script

1. Build your spl/u-boot normally.

1.1 git clone https://github.com/ADLINK/u-boot.git -b lf_v2022.04/sp2-imx8mp

1.2 enable CONFIG_IMX_HAB and set CONFIG_LPDDR4_ALL

# echo "CONFIG_IMX_HAB=y" >> configs/adlink_sp2imx8mp_defconfig
# echo "CONFIG_LPDDR4_ALL=y" >> configs/adlink_sp2imx8mp_defconfig

# make adlink_sp2imx8mp_defconfig
# make

2 run ./install_uboot_imx8.sh script to generate signed flash.bin

2.1 clean the build directory

# ./install_uboot_imx8.sh -c

2.1 build and sign flash.bin

# ./install_uboot_imx8.sh -s -b sp2imx8mp.dtb

NOTE: You may need to install extra library packages to successfully build all
      the required components. i.e. atf, optee, ddr/hdmi firmware, cst, imx-mkimage.

2.2 to re-use your existing PKI keys/crts to sign flash.bin.

# rm -fr build_fw_imx8/release/keys/*
# rm -fr build_fw_imx8/release/crts/*
# cp -fr <YOUR KEYS>/* build_fw_imx8/release/keys/
# cp -fr <YOUR CRTS>/* build_fw_imx8/release/crts/

remove the previous signed flash.bin

# rm -fr build_fww_imx8/imx-mkimage

then run the script again

# ./install_uboot_imx8.sh -s -b sp2imx8mp.dtb

The signed flash.bin is located at build_fw_imx8/imx-mkimage/iMX8M/flash.bin.signed

